Z||000001||cadero2dmax||11-11-2001||07:42 AM||||You can usually find 358ci, 650+ hp late model stock car engines, (in every condition from new to wore out) at:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.latemodeldigest.net/class.html" TARGET=_blank>www.latemodeldigest.net/class.html</A> <P>A couple times this summer I drove a Grand Prix bodied GT-1 version of a late model at Hallet, a road racing course here in Oklahoma. What a thrill. I have been racing for years, and that still was too much car for me :-(<P>You wouldn't want to try to run this type motor on the streets, however :-)<P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>86 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||1
